{\b NTSCRT plug-in for DaVinci Resolve}\par
This installer downloads the {\b latest release} of the NTSCRT OpenFX plug-in from github.com/anthonymendez/NTSCRT-Plugins and installs it into C:\\Program Files\\Common Files\\OFX\\Plugins. It needs an internet connection.\par
Quit DaVinci Resolve first (or restart it afterwards), then find the effect under Effects > OpenFX > Filters > NTSCRT.\par
{\b Updating:} run this installer again, or use {\i Update NTSCRT plug-in} in the Start menu.\par
{\b Uninstalling:} remove "NTSCRT plug-in installer" in Settings > Apps. That also removes the plug-in.\par
NTSCRT-Plugins is a port of NTSCRT by Finn McKenty. NTSCRT is free software under the MIT licence (Copyright (c) 2026 Anthony Mendez and Finn McKenty). It includes third-party components under their own licences: librashader (MPL-2.0, a separate library) and RetroArch CRT shaders (several under the GPL, separate shader files). See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the licenses folder inside the installed plug-in, or github.com/anthonymendez/NTSCRT-Plugins. Tick the box below to continue.\par
